/*1975. Maximum Matrix Sum
LeetCode Link:https://leetcode.com/problems/maximum-matrix-sum/?envType=daily-question&envId=2026-01-05
You are given an n x n integer matrix. You can do the following operation any number of times:

Choose any two adjacent elements of matrix and multiply each of them by -1.
Two elements are considered adjacent if and only if they share a border.

Your goal is to maximize the summation of the matrix's elements. Return the maximum sum of the matrix's elements using the operation mentioned above.

Approach:
Flipping two adjacent elements preserves the parity of negative numbers, so we can’t remove a single negative.
(+ , +) → (- , -)

(- , -) → (+ , +)

(+ , -) → (- , +)
To maximize the sum, take the absolute value of every element and add them all.

If the number of negative elements is even, all values can be made positive.

If the number of negatives is odd, one element must remain negative.

To minimize loss, make the smallest absolute value negative.

Final answer = sum of absolute values − 2 × smallest absolute value (only if negatives are odd).
*/

/**
 * @param {number[][]} matrix
 * @return {number}
 */
var maxMatrixSum = function(matrix) {
    let n=matrix.length;
    let sum=0;
    let negC=0;
    let minAbs = Infinity;
    for(let r of matrix){
        for(let c of r){
            sum+=Math.abs(c);
            if(c<0)negC++;
            minAbs=Math.min(minAbs,Math.abs(c));
        }
    }
    if(negC%2==1){
        sum-=2*minAbs;
    }
    return sum;
};
